# Day 24 - Users and Groups

## Commands Learned

- whoami
- id
- cat /etc/passwd | head
- cat /etc/group | head
- groups
- sudo useradd testuser
- sudo passwd testuser
- sudo userdel testuser

## What I Learned

Linux uses users and groups to manage access to files and system resources.

Each user has a unique User ID (UID), and groups help organize permissions for multiple users.

I learned how to view user accounts, inspect group information, create a user, assign a password, and remove a user.

## Key Concepts

- Users identify people or services on a system.
- Groups simplify permission management.
- Every user has a UID and belongs to one or more groups.
- Cloud engineers manage users to control server access.
